[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3193476484","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104518#issuecomment-3193476484","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104518","id":3193476484,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-WJWE","user":{"login":"rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229837?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing","html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-16T07:45:04Z","updated_at":"2025-08-16T07:45:04Z","body":"Here's a naive idea I had to reduce boilerplate for users: use the same RID for the visual instance and the FTI instance, and refer to both as an \"instance with FTI\". The RID will refer to the visual instance, so the existing `instance_` methods will work, and extra `instance_with_fti_` methods access the extra FTI data that is stored separately. You would have:\r\n- `instance_with_fti_create`\r\n- `instance_with_fti_set_transform`\r\n- `instance_with_fti_reset`\r\n\r\nThis sounds like a pretty nice API to me but the implementation wouldn't work the same as the current one with `id()`, so maybe it would be less efficient. Also maybe it would add overhead to `free_rid` for instances, but this could be worked around by adding an extra method like `instance_with_fti_clear` that would be required to call before `free_rid`.\r\n\r\nDo you think there's a way to make something like this work?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3193476484/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3193517107","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104518#issuecomment-3193517107","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104518","id":3193517107,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-WTQz","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-16T09:07:54Z","updated_at":"2025-08-16T09:08:27Z","body":"> Do you think there's a way to make something like this work?\r\n\r\nI did initially look at this but there are a couple of restrictions:\r\n* There are already quite a few existing `instance` API functions, and we want to avoid duplicating these\r\n* Ideally we don't want to introduce any new code in the existing `instance`, both in terms of slowing down, and also in terms of making the code more complex for `instances`, when we are fixing up a rare use case\r\n* Minimal maintenance is good\r\n\r\nI'll try and have another look at this.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3193517107/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3441876827","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104518#issuecomment-3441876827","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104518","id":3441876827,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7NJt9b","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-24T08:44:38Z","updated_at":"2025-10-24T08:45:17Z","body":"Ok I've thought of a alternative which may be better from a user perspective (not sure) .. so opinions welcome.\r\n\r\nThe issue is the lifetime of both the `fti_instance` and the `instance` need to be managed. In the first go (above) they are managed independently by the user.\r\n\r\nAn alternative may be when creating an `fti_instance` it automatically creates an `instance` in the background for you, and deletes it when you delete `fti_instance`.\r\n\r\nThere are two gotchas as a result:\r\n* you would need to call a function specifically to retrieve the `instance` RID from the `fti_instance` (e.g. `fti_instance_get_instance` .. which in itself is rather confusing :grinning: ), so you could then perform regular `instance` calls...\r\n* you would have to be sure not to `free` the `instance` that is returned above, otherwise you would get a double delete.\r\n\r\nLet me know if this is preferred. Perhaps I can create this as a separate PR to make it easier to see.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3441876827/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3455979624","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104518#issuecomment-3455979624","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104518","id":3455979624,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7N_hBo","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-28T11:25:30Z","updated_at":"2025-10-28T11:25:30Z","body":"Closing for now in favour of #112119.\r\n\r\nThis can be re-opened if desired, the new PR mentioned handles more cases (especially with FTI off) and should be easier in terms of use.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3455979624/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]